WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.516 --> 00:00:19.401
I called Theodoros, and I was born 52 years ago here on Chios, the fifth-largest Greek island in

2
00:00:19.441 --> 00:00:20.261
a large sea.

3
00:00:20.921 --> 00:00:26.623
Chios has been home to illustrious people such as the poet Homer, and the island is the only

4
00:00:26.723 --> 00:00:30.524
place on earth that grows mastic trees, which produce gum.

5
00:00:31.564 --> 00:00:37.748
But perhaps the island's greatest achievement is that it is the home of Greece's finest red wine.

6
00:00:39.309 --> 00:00:43.111
I am a winemaker, as my grandfather and father were before me.

7
00:00:43.751 --> 00:00:49.575
For over one hundred years, my family has taken care of this vineyard, and we have produced our

8
00:00:49.715 --> 00:00:50.275
own wine.

9
00:00:51.015 --> 00:00:58.540
But this year, 355 BC, I am ready to pass on the family legacy to my son Theodorakis,

10
00:00:59.260 --> 00:01:01.942
so he can carry on our winemaking tradition.

11
00:01:03.262 --> 00:01:09.746
Legend says that, long ago, the grandson of King Minos of Crete came to Chios and taught the

12
00:01:09.786 --> 00:01:11.086
people how to make wine.

13
00:01:11.907 --> 00:01:17.110
I do not know if that is true, but wine has been an integral part of Greek culture

14
00:01:17.270 --> 00:01:18.330
for hundreds of years.

15
00:01:19.051 --> 00:01:28.036
This wonderful drink is associated with Dionysus, the god of wine, who inspires artists, philosophers, and ordinary people

16
00:01:28.176 --> 00:01:28.516
like me.

17
00:01:29.268 --> 00:01:35.892
We hold many celebrations in his honor, and naturally wine is a major part of the festivities.

18
00:01:36.813 --> 00:01:42.436
Wine grapes love to grow in Chios, because of the weather and the island's many rolling hills.

19
00:01:43.236 --> 00:01:48.920
We plant the vines in the valleys, where they receive ample sunlight and good natural irrigation when it

20
00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:58.193
rains. Our island has warm days and cool nights, perfect weather for ripening grapes, and my ancestors developed

21
00:01:58.233 --> 00:02:01.456
a growing system long ago that takes advantage of this climate.

22
00:02:02.336 --> 00:02:07.160
Since I was very young, I have always carefully monitored my family's vineyard.

23
00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:14.345
Grapevines have several important parts, and I must pay close attention to each part for a successful crop.

24
00:02:15.005 --> 00:02:20.729
The trunk serves the same purpose as the trunk of a tree, providing firm support for the plant.

25
00:02:21.570 --> 00:02:29.508
In Chios we keep the trunk very short, about 55 centimeters high, because the earth provides warmth for

26
00:02:29.528 --> 00:02:31.250
the vine during the cool nights.

27
00:02:32.170 --> 00:02:36.794
The head is the main branch of the grapevine at the top of the trunk, where three or

28
00:02:36.874 --> 00:02:38.696
four canes grow each year.

29
00:02:39.436 --> 00:02:44.560
The delicious grapes grow on these canes, which I prune at the end of the growing season.

30
00:02:45.261 --> 00:02:51.206
The spurs are other thinner branches that develop at the top of the trunk, and I prune these

31
00:02:51.266 --> 00:02:53.768
back to short stubs at the end of the season too.

32
00:02:54.628 --> 00:03:01.612
Making wine is a long and tedious process, and a winemaker must be patient, hardworking, and diligent.

33
00:03:02.493 --> 00:03:09.637
Before harvesting the grapes, we have to clean large wooden vats with boiled seawater, as it is important

34
00:03:09.717 --> 00:03:12.879
that the grapes are stored in the cleanest containers possible.

35
00:03:13.580 --> 00:03:19.283
It takes many days to clean the vats, and then they must be completely dry before we put

36
00:03:19.323 --> 00:03:20.124
the grapes in them.

37
00:03:21.172 --> 00:03:27.654
In my vineyard each cluster of grapes is picked by hand, gathered in big baskets, and then thrown

38
00:03:27.694 --> 00:03:28.654
into a large vat.

39
00:03:29.475 --> 00:03:32.155
I have more than twenty workers who harvest the grapes.

40
00:03:32.976 --> 00:03:37.917
When the grapes have been harvested, children arrive and climb into the large vats of grapes.

41
00:03:38.817 --> 00:03:42.618
The fun begins when they start stomping on the grapes with their bare feet.

42
00:03:43.359 --> 00:03:47.660
Of course I remind them to wash their little feet before they jump into the vats!

43
00:03:48.564 --> 00:03:53.966
Many of them play games or sing as they crush the grapes into juice and pulp, a mixture

44
00:03:54.046 --> 00:03:54.867
called must.

45
00:03:55.787 --> 00:03:59.709
We put the must into clay jars, where it ferments for a long time.

46
00:04:00.449 --> 00:04:06.271
During fermentation the must foams up as the sugar in the grapes gradually turns to alcohol.

47
00:04:07.052 --> 00:04:14.295
But exposure to the air can make the must turn acidic, so I add honey and salt to

48
00:04:14.335 --> 00:04:16.856
keep the taste sweet and full of flavor.

49
00:04:17.580 --> 00:04:23.202
These ingredients make it easier to adjust the taste of the wine as it ferments, a process that

50
00:04:23.222 --> 00:04:24.322
takes about six months.

51
00:04:25.162 --> 00:04:31.164
When the wine is ready, I get the containers for the wine, called amphorae, delivered to my vineyard.

52
00:04:32.024 --> 00:04:37.226
An amphora is a tall ceramic vase with a handle on each side that makes it easy to

53
00:04:37.266 --> 00:04:44.608
carry. Amphorae provide excellent storage for the wine, and our amphorae are made in the village by Petros,

54
00:04:44.948 --> 00:04:45.608
a good friend.

55
00:04:46.416 --> 00:04:52.000
On one handle of each amphora is our special stamp, which shows the origin of the wine and

56
00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:53.061
the winemaker's name.

57
00:04:53.901 --> 00:04:57.904
So whoever drinks the wine will know where it came from and who made it.

58
00:04:59.005 --> 00:05:02.587
Ah! Here is Petros, just in time with the amphorae!

59
00:05:03.568 --> 00:05:04.288
But wait a moment.

60
00:05:04.869 --> 00:05:09.332
Before I pour the wine into the vases, I must make sure it is ready.

61
00:05:10.152 --> 00:05:15.456
I scoop some wine into a silver cup, dilute it with seawater, and swirl it around.

62
00:05:16.204 --> 00:05:23.588
Here in Chios wine tastes best when diluted, and the sea provides us with exactly what we need

63
00:05:23.848 --> 00:05:25.969
to make the wine even more delicious.

64
00:05:27.930 --> 00:05:35.074
Some barbarians drink the wine straight from the amphora, but this practice is frowned upon by polite society.

65
00:05:35.695 --> 00:05:38.916
Drinking pure wine marks one as an uncultured brute.

66
00:05:39.617 --> 00:05:42.198
But let us not dwell on anything unpleasant!

67
00:05:42.878 --> 00:05:47.297
This is my favorite part of making wine—tasting it.

68
00:05:49.058 --> 00:05:51.339
The aroma is already enticing.

69
00:05:52.340 --> 00:05:54.061
Ah, the first sip.

70
00:05:55.482 --> 00:05:57.223
Yes, it is perfect.

71
00:05:59.344 --> 00:06:06.268
I give permission, and my workers now pour the fermented wine through a cloth into the amphorae, and

72
00:06:06.308 --> 00:06:09.050
the cloth strains any pulp left over from the must.

73
00:06:09.830 --> 00:06:12.592
Theodoros' wine is now ready to be exported.

74
00:06:13.236 --> 00:06:16.139
However, the wine must be drunk within four years.

75
00:06:17.140 --> 00:06:22.184
If not, it will turn into vinegar, which no living creature can stand to swallow.

76
00:06:24.466 --> 00:06:29.931
After the amphorae are filled with wine, they are loaded onto ships and delivered to cities all around

77
00:06:29.991 --> 00:06:31.052
the interior sea.

78
00:06:31.812 --> 00:06:38.778
The finest red wines of Chios are truly appreciated by the nobility and elite of Greece, as well

79
00:06:38.839 --> 00:06:40.180
as those of Persia and Egypt.

80
00:06:40.756 --> 00:06:47.421
However, as Greek wine is gaining popularity every year, we hope to expand our shipping to lands even

81
00:06:47.601 --> 00:06:48.342
farther away.

82
00:06:49.723 --> 00:06:54.506
It is true that many people from other parts of the world are now cultivating their own grapes

83
00:06:54.546 --> 00:06:55.187
to make wine.

84
00:06:55.907 --> 00:07:01.911
But no other country will be able to grow grapes that surpass those from the vineyards of Chios!
